t3.micro       → General purpose
t3.medium      → General purpose
c7i.large      → Compute optimized
r7i.large      → Memory optimized

Interview answer:

EC2 instance types are different hardware configurations optimized for different workloads, such as general purpose, compute, memory, storage, and accelerated computing.

14. What is an AMI?

AMI = Amazon Machine Image.

An AMI is a template used to create an EC2 instance.

It contains things such as:

Operating system
Software/configuration
Root volume information

Example:

AMI
 ↓
Ubuntu + required configuration
 ↓
Create EC2
 ↓
EC2 Instance

AWS provides AMIs such as Ubuntu and Amazon Linux, and you can also create your own custom AMI.

Interview answer:

An AMI is a template containing the information required to launch an EC2 instance.

15. Difference between Stopping and Terminating an EC2 Instance
Stop

When you stop an instance:

Running
   ↓
Stopped

The instance is shut down, but you can start it again.

Example:

EC2 Running
     ↓ Stop
EC2 Stopped
     ↓ Start
EC2 Running
Terminate

When you terminate an instance:

Running
   ↓
Terminated

The instance is permanently deleted and cannot be started again.

Easy difference
Stop	Terminate
Temporarily shuts down	Permanently deletes instance
Can start again	Cannot start again
